{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase-1 RCA confirmed by Gerrit Verify run 31846417650 (macOS job 94913955831). Dynamic nested timing emitted `socket.getfqdn elapsed=35.013s`, `threading_http_server_constructor elapsed=35.014s`, and surrounding `_server fixture_setup elapsed=35.020s` for `test_server_binds_loopback_only`; TCP bind emitted nothing above the 1s threshold. This confirms CPython ThreadingHTTPServer construction synchronously performs reverse-DNS lookup of numeric loopback and rules out TCP bind, `_no_repo_commits`, tmp_path, and generic worker starvation for this recurring fixed ~35s phase. The overall run was 29m47s and macOS job 28m06s; default suite 23m25s and integration 2m38s. No other individual operation/test crossed 30s in the observed macOS default-tier timing. Defect legitimacy: defect/performance regression against the operator requirement that individual tests be negligible and CI average remain 20–30m without coverage loss. OSS precedent is strong: pip patches `socket.getfqdn` in its HTTP test server due to the same ~30s reverse-DNS delay; aiohttp and urllib3 bind literal loopback/raw sockets without this lookup. Observability change e88b8c6b83 received LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 and merged as Gerrit 1793 at 2026-08-14T22:54:08Z. A separate RED/GREEN fix ticket will preserve literal-loopback server semantics while eliminating the irrelevant reverse lookup."},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786748080150186001,"uuid":"5e77350d-2a47-410e-b505-719c1d52a8ab"}